\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A separating inequality holds for the target integer hull and is violated by a specified outside point. A Chvatal-Gomory cut rounds an appropriate rational combination of linear constraints to an integer-valid bound; RLT forms valid products of bounded constraints.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The supplied notation $q\in\mathbb R[x]^k$ and $q$ is SOS is ambiguous, and several practical targets lack quantitative criteria. The bundle is retained verbatim, without silently selecting one subproblem or defining the omitted SOS hierarchy.

Source-record limitation: The SOS denominator hierarchy is malformed: its notation is not defined, and zero multipliers make the written condition trivial without the omitted nontriviality restriction.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Are the intermediate SOS sets $\Sigma^k_{n,d}=\{p:\exists q\in\mathbb{R}[x]^k,\ q\text{ is SOS and }pq\text{ is SOS}\}$ convex? What is the complexity of selecting $s_i\in S_i$ such that $0\in\operatorname{conv}\{s_0,\ldots,s_d\}$? What are the complexities of finding a separating Chvátal–Gomory inequality and of integer quadratic optimization in dimension $3$? What practical rules govern combined SDP and RLT cuts? What practical algorithm solves evaluation-oracle mixed-integer optimization? Is the convex hull of a polyhedron minus finitely many polyhedra polyhedral? Which convex mixed-integer classes admit exact convexification? \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2015/46}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
The supplied catalogue labels this source record open; that metadata was checked against the supplied snapshot on 2026-10-11. The label is preserved for provenance and is not an independent verification of present open status or mathematical correctness. The catalogue literature assessment is dated 2026-08-21.

